From: osquera <github@alias.osquera.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARA: Stop reading access rules when GET DATA (next) is empty

Some SIMs (seen with a 9eSIM card) answer GET DATA (next) with 9000 and
no data. The loop then never reaches the announced length and sends the
command forever, so every caller of the service waits forever. NFC asks
isNfcEventAllowed() while holding its service lock, so NFC, Settings'
connected devices page and the Quick Settings tiles hang with it.

Treat an empty answer as an error, like any other failed read: the ARA
is then unusable on that SIM and calls fail fast instead of hanging.

---
  src/com/android/se/security/ara/AccessRuleApplet.java | 5 +++++
  1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/com/android/se/security/ara/AccessRuleApplet.java b/src/com/android/se/security/ara/AccessRuleApplet.java
index d23c68d..d13d911 100644
--- a/src/com/android/se/security/ara/AccessRuleApplet.java
+++ b/src/com/android/se/security/ara/AccessRuleApplet.java
@@ -108,6 +108,11 @@ public class AccessRuleApplet {
                 response = send(apdu);
                 // OK
                 if (response.isStatus(0x9000)) {
+                    // Some SIMs answer GET DATA (next) with 9000 but no data; without this check
+                    // the loop never ends and every caller, NFC included, waits forever.
+                    if (response.getData().length == 0) {
+                        throw new AccessControlException("GET DATA (next) returned no data.");
+                    }
                     try {
                         stream.write(response.getData());
                     } catch (IOException e) {
